<p>
Well this is awkward timing. No sooner had I finished bolting worktree management onto built-in <code>vc</code> than I installed the bleeding edge and found Emacs 31 went and did it properly. Right there in the 31 NEWS: a whole <code>C-x v w</code> working-tree map. So before I get too attached to my own code I thought I had better do an honest head-to-head. Verdict up front: I am keeping mine, with one key moved. Here is why.
</p>


